<p>
  This is the "about once a month" note from when you signed up.
</p>

<p>
  One thing worth knowing if you are caring for a parent at a distance: a
  missed reminder is not usually a crisis. People forget to press a button far
  more often than they forget the thing itself, so it is worth a quick call
  before assuming the worst. Remindly's missed-dose email only ever says what
  actually happened — nobody pressed Done — never that a dose was skipped.
</p>

<p>
  What has changed since you signed up: Remindly now rings your parent's own
  telephone, a landline or a mobile in the US or Canada, and says the reminder
  out loud. They press 1 to hear it and 1 when it is done, so nothing else is
  needed in the house. You can set it all up yourself, with no account or code
  for them to deal with; the first call says who set it up and asks them to
  agree. And starting is simpler: press "Set up reminders for my parent" on the
  website, and the link we email you creates your account.
</p>

<p>
  That is all — one note a month, nothing else.
  <a href="<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/subscribers/unsubscribe/#{@subscriber.signed_id(purpose: :unsubscribe)}" %>">Unsubscribe</a>
  any time, or just reply to this email to stop.
</p>

<p>
  <a href="<%= ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST %>">Remindly</a>
</p>
